                "1": {
                        "q": "What is a Hackathon?",
                        "a": "A hackathon is a combination of the words 'hack' and 'marathon'. In TeenAIgers, participants will complete a full project development process from idea to prototype with their team."
                },
                "2": {
                        "q": "Do I need programming skills to participate?",
                        "a": "Not necessarily. Although preferred, we welcome high school students with various skillsets, including but not limited to UI/UX design, product design, business, presentation. The only requirement is a enthusiam for technology and AI."
                },
                "3": {
                        "q": "Is the event online or offline?",
                        "a": "TeenAIgers is a hybrid hackathon with both offline days to the full hackathon experience and online sessions to ensure flexibility for non-local students."
                },
                "4": {
                        "q": "Are there any participation fees?",
                        "a": "TeenAIgers is free for all participants. We aim to eliminate economic barriers to allow more talented students to participate in this event."
                },
                "5": {
                        "q": "What rewards do winning teams receive?",
                        "a": "Winning teams will receive cash prizes, media exposure opportunities, and chances to connect with investors. Specific awards will be announced before the event."
                },
                "6": {
                        "q": "How will submissions be assessed?",
                        "a": "Projects will be judged on how well AI is utilized, innovation and creativity, and how effectively does it solve the problem. Check the judging rubric for more specific metrics :)"
                },
                "7": {
                        "q": "How do I register for TeenAIgers?",
                        "a": "If you are a student with one of our partnering schools, please find the teacher in charge to sign up. If you aren't, please fill out and submit the registration form on the 'Register' page of this website. We will review and notify results within 2 working days via email."
                },
                "8": {
                        "q": "Is there a theme?",
                        "a": "Yes, the theme for this hackathon is \"How to use technology, not used by technology.\""
                },
                "9": {
                        "q": "Will there be another hackathon?",
                        "a": "Yes, there will be several more hackathons that follow :D"
                },
                "10": {
                        "q": "How will I receive info during the hackathon?",
                        "a": "You will be informed through the organizing teacher of your school and through updates on our website."
                },
                "11": {
                        "q": "When is the hackathon?",
                        "a": "The hackathon dates are still TBD"
                }
